spoint git-from-sandbox HARD CONSTRAINT (2026-06-07, confirmed reproducibly): committing from the Linux sandbox to the mounted Windows folder C:\dev\spoint is IMPOSSIBLE. Every git index-WRITE (git add / git add --renormalize) corrupts .git/index to all-NUL ('error: bad signature 0x00000000; fatal: index file corrupt'), reproducibly, on each attempt. RECOVERY that works: rebuild the index read-only via `GIT_INDEX_FILE=.git/index.new git read-tree HEAD && mv -f .git/index.new .git/index` (mv is permitted where rm is NOT — 'Operation not permitted' on rm/unlink of .git/index, .git/index.lock, .git/objects/*). Stale .git/index.lock can be moved away with mv (not rm). But git status (read-only) works fine after an index rebuild. CONCLUSION: do ALL git writes (add/commit/push) on the Windows HOST, never the sandbox. The Edit/Write tools ALSO append trailing NUL padding to saved files on this folder (strip with python b.rstrip(b'\x00')). For spoint, treat the sandbox as read+edit-files-only; hand commits to the host.